**Remark 4.8 (Prior facts at length eight).** For the potential of Example 4.1 it was previously known that the potential is bad at every coupling and that the only matrices commuting with both $\Delta_8$ and $\operatorname{diag}(v)$ are scalars, so that it already answers the converse question of Lindblad and Guerrero negatively at length eight. Example 4.1 adds only the identification of its nodal factor through Theorem 3.2. Stance: repo-derived prior result, recorded without proof and not claimed as new in this volume.

